,30.9559],[-97.131,31.225],[-96.8841,31.5877],[-96.7984,32.0],[-96.8841,32.4123],[-97.131,32.775],[-97.5092,33.0441],[-98.3194,33.332],[-99.13,33.6199],[-99.9412,33.9078],[-100.7528,34.1958],[-101.565,34.4837],[-102.3777,34.7716],[-103.1909,35.0595],[-104.0047,35.3474],[-104.1489,35.3904],[-104.3023,35.3904],[-104.4464,35.3474],[-104.5639,35.2667],[-104.6406,35.1579],[-104.6673,35.0342]]]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"limit","holder":"texas","reach":0.0,"gapKm":1040.7,"cause":"river","causeText":"an unbridged crossing the column cannot supply across","consumer":"wendover-corridors"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.7,34.96]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"objective","ring":1,"subject":"Wendover","note":"what every column is reaching for. Nothing arrives.","consumer":"wendover-corridors"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-114.041,40.7365]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"objective","ring":2,"subject":"Wendover","note":"what every column is reaching for. Nothing arrives.","consumer":"wendover-corridors"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-114.041,40.7365]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"presence","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"ncr","reach":0.5,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"San Francisco","contestedPoint":1,"dispute":"A reader holds that the NCR had annexed all of western California by New Vegas; the sheet's author answers that there is no evidence for San Francisco, Arroyo, Modoc or Klamath being NCR controlled.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/locations.geojson#locations-san-francisco","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.437817,37.76149]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"presence","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"ncr","reach":0.7,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"Junktown","contestedPoint":2,"dispute":"Drawn as an NCR state. A reader answers that the NCR consists of its five initial states and several non-state territories; the author did not reply. Both agree the Republic is present - they disagree about what kind of holding it is.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/locations.geojson#locations-junktown","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.219549,35.601439]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"presence","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"ncr","reach":0.7,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"Bakersfield","contestedPoint":2,"dispute":"The same dispute as Junktown: drawn as an NCR state, contested as one in the thread and unanswered. The atlas's own placemark is Necropolis, the post-war Bakersfield.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/locations.geojson#locations-necropolis-formerly-bakersfield","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.024399,35.375349]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"presence","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"legion","reach":0.35,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"Yuma","contestedPoint":3,"dispute":"Drawn as Legion-held. A reader argues against it - the howitzer from there was SOLD to the Legion, which is trade rather than tenure. The author did not answer.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/locations.geojson#locations-yuma-proving-ground","precedence":2,"anchorNote":"The Yuma Proving Ground is the atlas's only present-day Yuma anchor; the ground the 2281 sheet letters YUMA is era geometry and an era layer never merges into the present. The mark is therefore about 80 km east of the city and is placed at community scale, which at this channel's own zooms is a few pixels."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-114.255409,33.01874]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"presence","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"legion","reach":0.35,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"Nipton","contestedPoint":4,"dispute":"Drawn as Legion-held. A reader answers that Nipton was torched and abandoned - a raiding camp, not a garrison. Unanswered.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/locations.geojson#locations-nipton","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-115.272567,35.467044]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"presence","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"legion","reach":0.2,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"Camp McCarran","contestedPoint":5,"dispute":"Drawn inside a Legion-influenced field. The Legion funded the Fiends through the Van Graffs, but the author states plainly that the Fiends have no loyalty to Caesar - and McCarran is an NCR garrison. Money reaches; nothing else does.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/locations.geojson#locations-camp-mccarran-formerly-mccarran-international-airport","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-115.158691,36.085315]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"presence","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"ncr","reach":0.35,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"Novac","contestedPoint":6,"dispute":"Drawn as held. A reader answers that Novac is independent, with possible NCR influence. Unanswered - and 'possible influence' is the exact claim this channel was adopted to be able to draw.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/locations.geojson#locations-novac","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-114.976301,35.729442]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"presence","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"ncr","reach":0.7,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"Vault City","contestedPoint":7,"dispute":"The 2253 sheet draws Vault City as an NCR holding. The long-standing reader objection is not that it is wrong but that New Reno is treated differently on the same sheet.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/locations.geojson#locations-vault-city","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.609084,41.23109]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"presence","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"ncr","reach":0.5,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"New Reno","contestedPoint":7,"dispute":"The other half of the Vault City objection: New Reno is NOT drawn as an NCR holding although readers place it in the same relationship to the Republic. Reach without control is what both sides are describing.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/locations.geojson#locations-new-reno","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.815769,39.534671]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"field","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"ncr","reach":0.5,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"The Shi","contestedPoint":1,"dispute":"The Republic of the Shi holds San Francisco. Whether that ground is inside the NCR is the collection's oldest west-coast argument, and it is the one place where the reach of one power over the territory of another can be drawn as an area rather than guessed at from a border.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/factions.geojson#factions-the-shi","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-122.51419,37.780639],[-122.506418,37.723601],[-122.495862,37.681432],[-122.494123,37.644007],[-122.461164,37.629054],[-122.440565,37.615185],[-122.403242,37.633797],[-122.391226,37.646303],[-122.37566,37.654272],[-122.374801,37.662833],[-122.383728,37.668541],[-122.380981,37.677372],[-122.387848,37.677236],[-122.393444,37.708761],[-122.377308,37.709033],[-122.375934,37.715551],[-122.382114,37.72044],[-122.378853,37.723155],[-122.361858,37.712835],[-122.359283,37.721933],[-122.356708,37.728315],[-122.374733,37.735375],[-122.367695,37.740058],[-122.376192,37.748678],[-122.376192,37.753021],[-122.385118,37.755464],[-122.380998,37.756278],[-122.383865,37.762743],[-122.388328,37.764914],[-122.386612,37.772513],[-122.379917,37.772106],[-122.38232,37.775091],[-122.390731,37.777398],[-122.384723,37.779433],[-122.385582,37.789066],[-122.390731,37.794356],[-122.400738,37.807561],[-122.411295,37.812172],[-122.420393,37.811358],[-122.446314,37.807561],[-122.465369,37.804848],[-122.470347,37.808646],[-122.477042,37.809731],[-122.477767,37.814464],[-122.478196,37.814413],[-122.47766,37.808785],[-122.4846,37.792944],[-122.492926,37.787722],[-122.499964,37.788671],[-122.506916,37.787722],[-122.512924,37.783652],[-122.51419,37.780639]]]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"form":"field","consumer":"contested-holdings","holder":"legion","reach":0.2,"control":false,"connected":true,"subject":"Fiends Territory","contestedPoint":5,"dispute":"The sheet washes the Fiends' ground as Legion-influenced. The Legion's money arrived through the Van Graffs; the author's own answer is that the Fiends have no loyalty to Caesar. A faint Legion stain over somebody else's ground is precisely that argument.","claimSource":"docs/changes/map-timeline/lore-contention-2026-08-14.md","geomSource":"geography/kml/factions.geojson#factions-fiends-territory-3b33123f","precedence":2},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-115.183471,36.090568],[-115.193957,36.097799],[-115.21284,36.101683],[-115.242365,36.103347],[-115.251975,36.120613],[-115.251288,36.132053],[-115.247342,36.142475],[-115.238417,36.153589],[-115.239445,36.163481],[-115.249915,36.171349],[-115.263193,36.176255],[-115.290688,36.174501],[-115.31103,36.162547],[-115.332744,36.148821],[-115.327977,36.125461],[-115.301245,36.114022],[-115.289401,36.083372],[-115.285624,36.051458],[-115.272578,36.029527],[-115.242805,36.007729],[-115.197144,36.00023],[-115.120143,36.005645],[-115.090617,36.01231],[-115.081347,36.021197],[-115.079974,36.033136],[-115.087784,36.037786],[-115.105465,36.041603],[-115.134734,36.047155],[-115.159625,36.051874],[-115.175589,36.055482],[-115.176447,36.064815],[-115.177735,36.073106],[-115.183471,36.090568]]]}}],"_consumers":{"wendover-corridors":"tools/build-influence-corridors.py","contested-holdings":"tools/build-influence-claims.py"},"_contestedPoints":{"1":"drawn - NCR presence at San Francisco and an NCR field over the Shi","2":"drawn - NCR presence at Junktown and Bakersfield","3":"drawn - Legion presence at Yuma","4":"drawn - Legion presence at Nipton","5":"drawn - Legion field over Fiends Territory and a Legion presence at Camp McCarran","6":"drawn - NCR presence at Novac","7":"drawn - NCR presence at Vault City and at New Reno","8":"NOT A FEATURE. 'Exact borders are anachronistic for a polity of a few hundred thousand' is the methodological criticism the channel answers by existing; there is no place to put a mark.","9":"ALREADY DRAWN, in the era channel. savannah-2313-influence-2313.geojson carries the six trading spheres with channel=influence. It is dated 2313 and the present day is 2296, so it cannot become a present-day claim until the channel takes date ranges.","10":"ALREADY DRAWN, in the era channel, as the same 2313 layer's Dissident belt. Same date obstacle as point 9.","11":"CANNOT YET. The 2290 sheet's lighter fills are author-confirmed influence, but the extraction reads that sheet's fills as one class. The technique exists - westcoast-2281-names.py measures a polygon's dominant fill and writes channelSuspect - and has never been run against the 2290 sheet.","12":"ALREADY DRAWN, in the era channel. ncr-2253-control-2253.geojson carries channel=deJure on 4 features and channel=deFacto on 28, which is the author's own intent. Dated 2253.","13":"CANNOT YET. The Deep South sheet's legend footnote denies that its borders imply governance, but no geometry from that sheet is extracted, so there is nothing to stain."}}
